\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. God of our fathers, unto Thee
\par Our fathers cried in danger's hour,
\par And then Thou gavest them to see
\par The acts of Thine almighty power.
\par They cried to Thee, and Thou didst hear;
\par They called on Thee, and Thou didst save;
\par And we their sons to-day draw near
\par Thy name to praise, Thy help to crave.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Lord, God of Hosts, uplift Thine hand,
\par Protect and bless our fatherland.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Thine is the majesty, O Lord,
\par And dine dominion over all;
\par When Thou commandest, at Thy word
\par Great kings and nations rise or fall.
\par For eastern realms, for western coasts,
\par For islands washed by every sea,
\par The praise be given, O God of Hosts,
\par Not unto us but unto Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Lord, God of Hosts, uplift Thine hand,
\par Protect and bless our fatherland.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. If in Thy grace Thou shouldst allow
\par Our fame to wax through coming days,
\par Still grant us humbly, then as now,
\par Thy help to crave, Thy name to praise.
\par Not all alike in speech or birth,
\par Alike we bow before Thy throne:
\par One fatherland throughout the earth
\par Our Father's noble acts we own.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Lord, God of Hosts, uplift Thine hand,
\par Protect and bless our fatherland.
\par Amen.
\par \f1 
